! =============================================================================
! SaltFoss Training — Segment 5 (0:40-0:52): Corrosion follows redox (3/3)
! =============================================================================
! F = 135.9 (near the UF4 endpoint, oxidizing). This is the money result:
! dissolved Cr rises ~8 ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE from 04_corrosion_reducing.ti to
! here, across what a salt chemist might consider a narrow redox window.
! Business takeaway: keep the UF4/UF3 buffer reduced and Cr stays in the
! alloy; let it oxidize and the structural material dissolves. This exact
! quantity becomes a boundary condition for a MOOSE corrosion model (next
! session).
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/saltfoss/04_corrosion_oxidizing.ti
! Verified output: Cr2+ = 2.87e-05,  Cr3+ = 1.35e-07
! Full trio summary (mol fraction Cr2+ in melt):
!   F=135.0 (reducing):  1.08e-14
!   F=135.5 (mid):       3.65e-07
!   F=135.9 (oxidizing): 2.87e-05        <- ~9 orders of magnitude rise
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 900
pressure          = 1.0
mass(3)           = 66.0       ! Li
mass(4)           = 33.0       ! Be
mass(92)          = 1.0        ! U
mass(24)          = 0.01       ! Cr  -- structural-alloy tracer
mass(9)           = 135.9      ! F   -- oxidizing (near UF4)
temperature unit  = K
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/MSD-TC_V4.1_Fluorides_No_Func.dat
print mode        = 2
